tes are secondary to actual research output. Published papers, strong research memos and credible internships can be more valuable indicators of ability."}]},{"heading":"PG Options","kind":"pg_india","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"LL.M"},{"type":"p","text":"Strong options include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Constitutional Law"},{"text":"Jurisprudence"},{"text":"Public Law"},{"text":"Human Rights Law"},{"text":"Administrative Law"},{"text":"Legal Theory"},{"text":"International Law"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Academic Research"},{"type":"flow","items":["LL.B","LL.M","Research Assistant / Research Fellow","Ph.D","Academic / Research Career"]},{"type":"h","text":"Other Options"},{"type":"p","text":"Depending on career direction:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Public Policy"},{"text":"Political Science"},{"text":"International Relations"},{"text":"Economics"},{"text":"Public Administration"},{"text":"Development Studies"},{"text":"Interdisciplinary education can be especially valuable for constitutional and policy research."}]}]},{"heading":"Career Specialisations","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Constitutional Researcher"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Fundamental rights"},{"text":"Judicial review"},{"text":"Federalism"},{"text":"Separation of powers"},{"text":"Constitutional interpretation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Judicial Research"},{"type":"p","text":"Support judges/research offices, where eligible, with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Case research"},{"text":"Precedent analysis"},{"text":"Comparative law"},{"text":"Legal memoranda"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Legislative Researcher"},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Bills"},{"text":"Legislation"},{"text":"Parliamentary materials"},{"text":"Policy implications"},{"text":"Regulatory frameworks"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Policy Researcher"},{"type":"p","text":"Work on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Public policy"},{"text":"Governance"}