t":"│ └── Separation of Powers"},{"text":"│"},{"text":"├── Jurisprudence"},{"text":"│ ├── Legal Positivism"},{"text":"│ ├── Natural Law"},{"text":"│ ├── Legal Realism"},{"text":"│ └── Critical Legal Theory"},{"text":"│"},{"text":"├── Research"},{"text":"│ ├── Case-Law Research"},{"text":"│ ├── Statutory Research"},{"text":"│ ├── Comparative Law"},{"text":"│ ├── Legislative Research"},{"text":"│ └── Policy Research"},{"text":"│"},{"text":"├── Writing"},{"text":"│ ├── Research Memos"},{"text":"│ ├── Case Briefs"},{"text":"│ ├── Legal Articles"},{"text":"│ └── Academic Papers"},{"text":"│"},{"text":"├── Technology"},{"text":"│ ├── Legal Databases"},{"text":"│ ├── Research Tools"},{"text":"│ ├── Citation Management"},{"text":"│ └── AI-Assisted Research"},{"text":"│"},{"text":"└── Professional Skills"},{"text":"├── Critical Thinking"},{"text":"├── Analytical Reasoning"},{"text":"├── Attention to Detail"},{"text":"├── Communication"},{"text":"└── Presentation"}]}]},{"heading":"Best Overall Positioning","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The strongest positioning for this career is:"},{"type":"p","text":"“Legal researcher specialising in constitutional law, jurisprudence, case-law analysis and public-law research.”"},{"type":"p","text":"For this pathway, research output is the strongest differentiator. A student who graduates with a portfolio of well-researched case briefs, constitutional research papers, legal memoranda, comparative-law studies and legislative analyses will be much better positioned than someone whose profile consists only of coursework and certificates."},{"type":"p","text":"The ideal long-term combination is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Constitutional Law","Jurisprudence","Research Methodology","Legal Writing","Primary-Source Research","LegalTech/AI Research Skills."],"sep":"+"}]}]}